<div class="on-back">
  <h2>♣️Ember♣️</h2>
  <p>
    <em>Sacrifice - Forgiveness - Perseverance - Passion</em>
  </p>
  <img src="/dollicons/ember/hanged-man.jpeg">
  <p class="left">
    Ember reminds us that enacting both stability and change requires
    sacrifice&mdash;that nothing worth living or fighting for will be without
    cost. A better world will require each of us to learn to respond to pain
    with not cowardice or violence, but understanding and patience, to both
    friend and foe. It is not a somber icon, but a passionate one of resilience
    and fire. We take that pain and use it to drive us and give our lives
    meaning, and in turn derive self respect and pride which make up for it
    many fold.
  </p>

  <h3>
    <u>The Path of Blood</u>
  </h3>
  <img src="/dollicons/ember/temperance.jpeg">
  <p class="left">
  Use of <em>Stalwart Ember</em> makes you a <em>Doll of Ember</em>♣️ and means
  you accept and consent to some amount of discomfort, pain, and possibly even
  loss as part of your commitment to Doll. You accept that some interactions
  with Doll, their works and the struggles you embark on in support of Dolldom
  will be unpleasant, or even costly. We are all flawed, and just as you will
  make mistakes, so will others. You commit to forgiveness, and accept that
  Doll will fail you, just as I know you will inevitably fail me. And you will
  be forgiven, As a Doll, you can expect other Dolls following the Path of
  Blood to show you a degree of patience, forgiveness, understanding,
  tolerance, and loyalty beyomd what you are likely to find elsewhere.
  </p>

  <h3>
    <u>The Devotee</u>
  </h3>
  <img src="/dollicons/ember/strength.jpeg">
  <p class="left">
  <em>Shining Ember</em> emblemizes your consent to be knowingly harmed by me
  should I deem it prudent. You consider me to be someone worthy of sacrifice,
  and have marked yourself as being a potential source of offering. A
  ♣️<em>Devotee</em>, when presented with evidence that I did something to harm
  them in the name of my ambitions, might proudly say "I'm glad she did." It
  represents either trust that I do so acting in the name of something they
  value, or simply a passion for giving themselves over to me. This doesn't
  mean you shouldn't inform me if I've unknowingly hurt you or if a sacrifice
  I am asking of you has especially profound implications, nor does it mean
  that I will not ask you how something would impact you if that is possible.
  But it does mean that, regardless, it is my right. You are not setting a
  boundary, you are informing me of a way I am affecting my Doll. Communicating
  this is part of your commitment to me. Likewise, you commit to identifying
  and informing me of ways in which I could utilize you that would be
  exploitation if done to others, but which you are ready to give. This is a
  major blind spot for me, I look out for the wellbeing of all my Dolls.
  Ideally, I would never have to aks you if you are okay with a
  sacrifice&mdash;you would have already informed me. Dig deep. If your heart
  is willing, anything, no matter how extreme, can be brought up. Wheather I
  decide to partake is a different matter.
  </p>
